From ec216528a64dc3b1e7edbc4f99910ba7dea937ac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Keith Packard <keithp@keithp.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 23:53:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] libos/linux: Wait on each call_once flag separately

call_once held the global libc lock while its function ran. If the
function was cancelled the lock stayed held and the flag stayed set,
hanging every later libc lock user; POSIX requires the flag to be left
as if call_once had never been called. Callers using other flags also
waited for the function, so one that waited for another thread using
call_once deadlocked.

On Linux, keep the running thread's id in the flag and wait on it with
a futex, with a cleanup handler resetting it; a nested call on the
same flag still returns at once.
---
 libos/linux/call_once.c | 91 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 libos/linux/meson.build |  3 +-
 2 files changed, 93 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 libos/linux/call_once.c

diff --git a/libos/linux/call_once.c b/libos/linux/call_once.c
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000..a4608c86fc
--- /dev/null
+++ b/libos/linux/call_once.c
@@ -0,0 +1,91 @@
